.TH RGBDNS-ACME 1 "2026-08-18" "rgbdns 0.6.2"
.SH NAME
rgbdns-acme \- manage ACME DNS-01 TXT state through rgbdns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbdns-acme present
.BI --zone " zone " --name " owner " --value " token"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rgbdns-acme cleanup
.BI --zone " zone " --name " owner " --value " token"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rgbdns-acme clear
.BI --zone " zone " --name " owner"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rgbdns-acme list
.RI [ --zone " zone" ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rgbdns-acme
is the local administrative and ACME manual-hook interface for rgbdns.  Its
mutating commands send a TSIG-authenticated RFC 2136 UPDATE to the running
primary.  They therefore use the same authorization, durability, serial, live
publication, and AXFR path as Certbot's RFC 2136 plugin.
.PP
.B present
adds one TXT value without removing concurrent values.
.B cleanup
removes only the specified value.
.B clear
removes the authorized TXT RRset.
.B list
reads the durable generated overlay and does not reveal TSIG credentials.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Policy file.  The default is
.IR /etc/rgbdns/acme-update.conf .
.TP
.BI --server " address:port"
Primary update endpoint.  The default is
.IR 127.0.0.1:53 .
.TP
.BI --state-dir " directory"
State directory used by
.BR list .
The default is
.IR /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns .
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable output.
.SH SECURITY
The policy file contains TSIG secrets and must be readable only by root and the
rgbdns service group.  Use a separate key for each certificate host or trust
boundary.  Network keys are restricted to configured
.B _acme-challenge
TXT owners and cannot change ordinary zone data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rgbdns/acme-update.conf
TSIG keys and per-zone policies.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns/acme-overlay.data
Generated durable TXT overlay; do not edit.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rgbdns/tinydns/acme-serials
Generated per-zone serial state; do not edit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tinydns (1),
.BR rgbdns-setup (8),
.BR nsupdate (1)
